{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK72E2wK7djpvoCYbned","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the migration so it no longer fails when a proxy model already has permissions under its own content type. The existing `auth_tests.test_migrations` tests pass. I didn't add a test that reproduces the recreated-proxy case.\n\nThe change is in `django/contrib/auth/migrations/0011_update_proxy_permissions.py`. Before moving permissions from the concrete model's content type to the proxy's, the migration now excludes any codename the proxy's content type already has. That removes the duplicate-key `IntegrityError`.\n\nAny leftover permission rows on the old content type are not moved or deleted. They stay where they were."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1482,"cache_read_input_tokens":19326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1482},"output_tokens":204,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12b56368-be28-415b-9a12-1815ec1a9bcd","uuid":"c6bda652-3fdc-4b9a-8276-bc2534590a24","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:54:01.260Z","request_id":"req_011ChK72DuFjyPe1cxkhFWv6"}
